meta {
  name: Upload Attachment
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/storage/upload
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(notes/sample-attachment.txt)
  fileName: sample-attachment.txt
  fileSize: 59
  folder: notes/{{torgId}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.data && res.body.data.key) {
    bru.setEnvVar("attachmentKey", res.body.data.key);
  }
}

docs {
  Step 1 of attaching a file to a note: the existing storage upload (`StorageResource.uploadFile`). Notes
  only accept keys under `notes/<torgId>/`, so `folder` must be `notes/<your torgId>`.

  `fileName` and `fileSize` are required form fields even though `file` is sent: the key is built from
  `fileName` (the request fails without it) and `fileSize` is the byte count sent to storage, so it must
  match the file. The response `data` has `key` (send this with the note), `url` (a 10-minute link),
  `fileName`, `contentType`, `size`. The key is saved to `attachmentKey`.

  Roles: VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN, TRUCK_MANAGER, FUND_MANAGER, DRIVER, OPERATOR, ACCOUNTANT,
  FUEL_STATION_MANAGER, FUEL_STATION_ATTENDER. MANAGER and AGENT can use notes but can't upload here.
}
